74a2a6d422cbd35b5a135d63ff", "fixed_tree": "3b75fe89721763f7583dbf2116aee8de69f04281", "fixes": [{"commit": "c22e3bf9a2733274a2a6d422cbd35b5a135d63ff", "parent": "095738e7de5484aa34471fb056960d9463c44e85"}], "patch": "patches/c22e3bf9a2733274a2a6d422cbd35b5a135d63ff-1/20260924T002108Z-c74214aa.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "runs": {}, "test_sources": [{"commit": "c22e3bf9a2733274a2a6d422cbd35b5a135d63ff", "paths": ["rational/src/lib.rs"]}], "tests": ["test::test_signed"]}, "shard": "num-rational", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Correct Ratio::is_negative and Ratio::is_positive", "summary": "The parent implementation classifies 0/1 as positive, making signum() return 1 instead of 0; zero with a negative denominator is incorrectly classified as negative. The fix checks strictly positive or negative numerator/denominator combinations, excluding zero from both predicates. The upstream test extended by this fix first detects the regression at assert_eq!(_0.signum(), Zero::zero()). Select test::test_signed in the num-rational crate at rational/Cargo.toml. No tests were executed.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:23:19.966069+00:00"}
